6.11 Referential Integrity
The database enforces the following referential integrity constraints:

Every evidence.anomaly_id must exist in anomaly.

Every related_anomaly.anomaly_id and related_anomaly.related_anomaly_id must exist in anomaly.

Every stag_link.anomaly_id must exist in anomaly.

Every null_model_link.anomaly_id must exist in anomaly.

Every verification_link.anomaly_id must exist in anomaly.

Every lifecycle.anomaly_id must exist in anomaly.

Every provenance.anomaly_id must exist in anomaly.

Every moderation.anomaly_id must exist in anomaly.

The version chain (supersedes and superseded_by) must be acyclic.

The related-anomaly relation must be symmetric: if A is related to B, B must be related to A.

